# Corpora are NEVER committed.
#
# This is not only a size concern. Common Crawl's terms do not clearly permit
# redistributing derived datasets, and the project's answer is to publish the
# RECIPE rather than the data: a seeded sampler plus pinned crawl IDs lets a
# stranger rebuild the corpus (the phishing side byte for byte; the Common Crawl side by the
# same method, not the same sample: REPRODUCE.md 2a). Committing the URLs would quietly
# undo that decision (DESIGN.md, E0).
# Exclude the CONTENTS of data/, not the directory itself. Git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded, so a bare `data/` here would make
# the manifest exceptions below silently ineffective — and a `!data/` negation
# over-corrects and admits the entire ~1 GB corpus.
data/*
!data/corpus/
data/corpus/*

# Manifests ARE provenance, not data: they pin crawl IDs, seeds, feed HEADs and
# content hashes, and they are the recipe the release ships INSTEAD of the URLs.
!data/corpus/*.manifest.json

# The Common Crawl shard maps the extraction reads (which public suffixes live in which index
# shard). They are built by network probes that may miss a few shards, so a rebuilt map could
# differ; they are tracked so level 2a reproduces exactly (D2 step 6). Suffixes only, no URLs.
!data/corpus/shardmaps/

# Frozen splits are NOT tracked (D2 release audit, research/d2/AUDIT.md): they hold
# the corpus's registrable domains, real phishing domains among them. They are
# rebuilt deterministically from the recipe, and their manifests -- rule, seed,
# counts and content_sha256, no domains -- are tracked in
# data/corpus/splits.manifest.json, so a rebuilt split is still hash-verified.

# The generated statistics behind BENCHMARK.md — the document is derived from
# this file rather than transcribed, so the two cannot silently disagree.
!data/corpus/benchmark_stats.json

# The E1 baseline numbers BENCHMARK.md section 6 is derived from.
!data/corpus/baseline_e1.json

*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
